  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR does the five items of #2528 (follow-ups of #2504).\n\n1. **The Break-through note agrees with the field.** A Drill measured from its full diameter said \"through holes run 2.803 mm past the part bottom (Break-through)\" for a 1 mm Break-through. The note now says \"through holes run 2.803 mm past the part bottom (Break-through 1.000 mm from the full diameter, plus the 1.803 mm drill point), the deepest to Z-2.803\". `break_through::Broke` carries the point length (`with_point`). The Tip case, Bore and Thread keep \"(Break-through)\". The words \"run X past the part bottom\" stay, so readers of the note keep working.\n2. **The \"Break-through from\" selector is disabled where it has no effect.** `holes_page::break_through_from_idle` gives the reason, in the generator's order:\n   - a lathe's axial drill (it always measures to the tip);\n   - a stated Bottom;\n   - a Spot, Tap, Floating tap or Ream cycle (`drilling::through_tip_run`);\n   - no through hole in the list.\n\n   The combo is disabled. The reason shows when the user hovers the row (`on_disabled_hover_text`, the pattern of `fixture_menu.rs` and `feeds_page.rs`). A disabled widget shows no plain hover text, so the normal hint is used only while the row is enabled. I chose \"disable\" over \"hide\": a hidden row reads as a missing feature.\n3. **A correction to the #2441 decision entry.** Issue branches do not edit `RECOMMENDED.md`, so `docs/decisions/2528-drill-point-followups.md` records the correction:\n   - PR #2504 did not keep the examples byte-identical. It rebuilt the catalog case `2d/first-part` (`G73 ... Z-1. Q18.` to `G83 ... Z-2.803 Q6.`) and `examples/first-router-part.camproj` (v62 to v68, `full_diameter`, depth -1.0 to -2.802582). Only `examples/first-part.camproj` stayed the same.\n   - An MCP or script patch does not default to `FullDiameter`. `add_operation` starts from the seed (`FullDiameter`). `edit_operation` applies a JSON merge patch over the stored parameters, so an omitted `break_through_from` keeps the stored value.\n4. **Three file splits, structure only.** The `#[test]` counts do not change (app lib 322, motion lib 777 before item 1).\n   - `crates/app/src/stock_sim.rs` (469 lines): the program plan moves to `stock_sim_plan.rs` (225 + 256 lines).\n   - `crates/app/src/stock_play.rs` (409 lines): `PlayIndex` and `PlaySeed` move to `stock_play_index.rs` (330 + 93 lines). Their fields become `pub(super)`, because `FieldPlay` and `stock_play_head` read them.\n   - `crates/motion/src/drilling/tests.rs` (508 lines): the five recognition tests move to `tests_recognize.rs` (404 + 110 lines). The shared helpers stay, so the other test modules keep their imports.\n5. **Every post records a full-diameter through hole.** A new recorded stream `drill_full_diameter` (one 10 mm through hole, the default Full diameter, tip at Z-12.803) joins `recorded::CASES` and the `post_suite!` macro. Its generator guard is `recorded_post_streams::drill_full_diameter_stream_is_current`. The 15 mill posts record a program with `Z-12.803`. LinuxCNC and Heidenhain Klartext refuse it by name, as they refuse `drill_retract`. The lathe, wire, sinker, plasma and waterjet posts keep their named refusals.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. Item 5 adds 27 new goldens (`crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/<post>/drill_full_diameter.{nc,refusal}`) and one stream. No existing `.nc` golden changes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` lib: `break_through::tests::a_full_diameter_drill_names_the_field_and_its_point`.\n- `camcraft-app` `break_through`: `the_default_is_today_s_millimetre_and_is_said` (the note names 1.000 mm and the 1.803 mm point for the Full-diameter drill, and \"(Break-through)\" for Tip and Bore).\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: `holes_break_through::drill_break_through_from_is_disabled_where_it_has_no_effect` (the four reasons; the combo is disabled until a hole is through; a hover over the disabled row paints the reason, and a hover over the enabled row paints the normal hint). `drill_break_through_from_defaults_to_full_diameter_and_switches_to_tip` now gives the draft a through hole first.\n- `camcraft-app` `recorded_post_streams`: `drill_full_diameter_stream_is_current`.\n- `camcraft-post` `script_*`: `drill_full_diameter` in each of the 27 post suites.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate on 31438caa1 (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 393 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 49.5 min.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-post -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post` after the merge of `upstream/main` (with #4367): all pass, and no golden changes.\n- `#[test]` counts before and after the splits: app lib 322, motion lib 777.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`) on 31438caa1: 115 steps (1 build, 41 `motion`, 73 `app`), 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 73.0 min. The known fails #1950 (3) and #2849 (1) are red as expected.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe Levels group on the Heights tab of a Drill operation, with the pointer over \"Break-through from\".\n\n| No through hole: disabled, the reason on hover | A through hole: enabled, the normal hint |\n|---|---|\n| ![disabled](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2528/bt-from-disabled.png) | ![enabled](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2528/bt-from-enabled.png) |\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real machine.\n\nChangelog: Drill: the Break-through note names the field's value and the drill point apart for a full-diameter drill. The \"Break-through from\" choice is disabled, with the reason, where it has no effect (lathe axial drill, stated Bottom, spot/tap/ream cycles, no through hole).\n\nFixes #2528\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
